---
<div class="title">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="org">
          Fifth Wheel Supper Club, LLC d/b/a Fifth Wheel &middot; Atlanta,
          Georgia
        </p>
        <p class="updated">Last updated 5 September 2026</p>
        <p class="lede">
          This policy explains what we collect, why, who else sees it, how long
          we keep it, and what you can ask us to do with it. It applies to our
          website, our application forms, our text messages, and our events. If
          anything here is unclear, write to us and a person will answer.
        </p>
      </div>

      <main id="main">
        <div class="callout">
          <p>
            <strong>The short version.</strong> We collect what we need to seat
            you at a good table and to keep the table safe. Restaurants never
            learn who you are. Other guests never see your contact details or
            your votes. We do not sell your information, and we do not use it to
            advertise to you anywhere else.
          </p>
        </div>

        <section>
          <h2>
            <span class="num">Section 1</span>Who is responsible for your
            information
          </h2>
          <p>
            Fifth Wheel Supper Club, LLC, a Georgia limited liability company
            doing business as Fifth Wheel, is responsible for the personal
            information described in this policy. You can reach us at
            <a href="mailto:hello@5thwheel.app">hello@5thwheel.app</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Section 2</span>What we collect</h2>

          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Category</th>
                <th>What it includes</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Application</td>
                <td>
                  First name, email address, age range, who you would like to be
                  seated with, ages you are open to meeting, whether you are
                  looking for something casual or a relationship, whether you
                  want a surprise game at the table, neighborhoods you would
                  travel to, nights you are free, and how you heard about us.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Profile</td>
                <td>
                  Age, how you identify, who you are open to being seated with,
                  industry, interests, a one-line self-description, dietary
                  restrictions, and allergies.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Contact</td>
                <td>Mobile number and email address.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Verification</td>
                <td>
                  The result of your identity check &mdash; a pass or fail, and
                  the identifying details needed to confirm you.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Payments</td>
                <td>
                  Records of what you paid and when, and refunds. Card numbers
                  are handled by our payment processor and never reach us.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Events</td>
                <td>
                  Which tables you were seated at, whether you checked in, your
                  votes, resulting matches, and any feedback you give us
                  afterwards.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Reports</td>
                <td>
                  Anything you tell a coordinator about another guest, and
                  anything a coordinator logs about an evening.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Technical</td>
                <td>
                  Basic request logs and a session cookie that keeps you signed
                  in. Our landing page also loads the Meta Pixel, which tells
                  Meta that a visit or a waitlist signup happened so we can
                  measure our advertising. It never receives your name, email,
                  or anything you entered on the form.
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <h3>Sensitive information</h3>
          <p>
            Some of what we collect is treated as sensitive under privacy law
            &mdash; specifically, how you identify and who you are open to being
            seated with. We collect it for one reason: it is impossible to build
            a table of five people who might be interested in one another
            without it. We use it only to decide who sits together. We never
            disclose it to venues, never use it for advertising, and never sell
            or share it for anyone else&rsquo;s commercial purposes. You provide
            it voluntarily when you complete a profile, and you may ask us to
            delete it at any time, though we will not be able to seat you
            afterwards.
          </p>

          <h3>Identity documents</h3>
          <p>
            Identity verification is performed by a third-party provider. Your
            photo ID and any selfie you take are submitted directly to that
            provider and are processed under their controls.
            <strong
              >Fifth Wheel does not receive, store, or have access to images of
              your identity documents or your face.</strong
            >
            We receive the outcome of the check and the details necessary to
            confirm you are who you said you are.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Section 3</span>Why we use it</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>To seat you.</strong> Curating a table is the core of the
              Service, and it is what your profile exists for.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>To run the evening.</strong> Confirming your seat, sending
              you the address, reminding you, and collecting the vote.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>To take payment</strong> and to process refunds under the
              cancellation terms.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>To confirm you are real.</strong> Every guest at the table
              has been verified, which is what makes the format work.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>To keep the table safe.</strong> Reviewing reports, and
              deciding who is seated again.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>To improve.</strong> Understanding which venues and which
              pairings worked.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>To email you about new tables</strong>, if you asked us
              to. You can stop this at any time and it does not affect your
              booking messages.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>To meet legal obligations</strong>, including tax and
              accounting records.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Section 4</span>Who else sees it</h2>

          <h3>Venues</h3>
          <p>
            Restaurants and bars receive a confirmed party count, a reservation
            time, and the name Fifth Wheel. They do not receive guest names,
            contact details, photographs, ages, application answers, votes, or
            match outcomes. Where a table has an allergy or dietary requirement
            we pass that to the kitchen, and we do so without naming you
            wherever that is practical. This restriction is built into our
            systems, not merely promised.
          </p>

          <h3>Other guests</h3>
          <p>
            Before an evening, the four other guests know only that a table has
            been formed. Names and profile details are revealed at check-in, not
            before. Other guests never see your contact details unless a mutual
            match results and you choose to share them, and they never see your
            votes &mdash; a vote that is not mutual is never recorded as a
            result and is never disclosed to anyone.
          </p>

          <h3>Service providers</h3>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Provider</th>
                <th>What they handle</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Supabase</td>
                <td>Database and account hosting (United States)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Vercel</td>
                <td>Website hosting and delivery</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Stripe</td>
                <td>Card payments and refunds</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Stripe Identity</td>
                <td>
                  Identity verification, including document and selfie images
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Twilio</td>
                <td>Text messages, including verification codes</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Resend</td>
                <td>Email delivery</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Meta</td>
                <td>Advertising measurement on the landing page only</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p>
            Each receives only what it needs to do its job, and each is bound to
            use it only for that purpose.
          </p>

          <h3>Everyone else</h3>
          <p>
            We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it for
            cross-context behavioural advertising. We disclose information
            outside the above only where the law requires it, where it is
            necessary to protect someone&rsquo;s safety, or where a business is
            transferred &mdash; in which case this policy continues to apply.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Section 5</span>How long we keep it</h2>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Information</th>
                <th>Retention</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Waitlist entries</td>
                <td>
                  Until you ask us to remove you, or two years without contact
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Profile and account</td>
                <td>While your account is active, then 12 months</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Votes and matches</td>
                <td>12 months after the evening</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Payment and tax records</td>
                <td>7 years, as required by law</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Safety and conduct reports</td>
                <td>Up to 7 years, so patterns can be recognised</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Message delivery logs</td>
                <td>12 months</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p>
            When a retention period ends we delete the information or
            irreversibly anonymise it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Section 6</span>Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Whatever state or country you are in, we will honour the following.
            Write to
            <a href="mailto:hello@5thwheel.app">hello@5thwheel.app</a> and we
            will respond within 30 days.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Access.</strong> Ask what we hold about you and receive a
              copy.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Correction.</strong> Fix anything inaccurate. You can edit
              most of it yourself in your profile.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Deletion.</strong> Ask us to erase your information. We
              will, except for records we are legally required to keep and any
              safety report, which we retain in a minimised form.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Portability.</strong> Receive your information in a
              machine-readable format.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Opt out of marketing.</strong> Every marketing email
              carries an unsubscribe link that works immediately. Booking
              confirmations, address reveals, and refund notices are not
              marketing and continue regardless.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Limit sensitive information.</strong> Ask us to stop using
              how you identify or who you are open to meeting. We will honour
              it, and we will no longer be able to seat you.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>No retaliation.</strong> Exercising any of these rights
              will never affect how you are treated.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We do not require you to create an account to exercise these rights,
            and we will not charge you for it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Section 7</span>Text messages</h2>
          <p>
            When you book a seat, you agree to receive text messages about that
            booking &mdash; confirmation, the address on the day, a reminder,
            the ballot prompt, and your result. Reply <strong>STOP</strong> to
            any message to opt out. Opting out of texts means we cannot send you
            the address of your table, so please tell us if you do. Message and
            data rates may apply.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Section 8</span>Security</h2>
          <p>
            Information is encrypted in transit and at rest. Access is
            restricted to coordinators who need it, and reports and votes are
            restricted further still &mdash; votes are not readable by any
            guest, including the person who cast them, and reports are visible
            only to a coordinator. No system is perfectly secure, and we will
            tell you promptly if a breach affects your information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Section 9</span>Age</h2>
          <p>
            Fifth Wheel is for adults aged 21 and over. We do not knowingly
            collect information from anyone under 21. If we learn that we have,
            we delete it. If you believe a minor has given us information, write
            to us.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>
            <span class="num">Section 10</span>Where your information is held
          </h2>
          <p>
            We operate in the United States and our providers store information
            in the United States. If you use the Service from elsewhere, you
            understand your information will be processed here, under United
            States law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Section 11</span>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy. The date at the top always reflects the
            current version. If a change materially affects how we use your
            information, we will tell you by email or text before it takes
            effect.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2><span class="num">Contact</span>Questions about your privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Fifth Wheel Supper Club, LLC d/b/a Fifth Wheel &middot; Atlanta,
            Georgia<br />
            <a href="mailto:hello@5thwheel.app">hello@5thwheel.app</a> &middot;
            <a href="https://5thwheel.app">5thwheel.app</a>
          </p>
          <p>
            A person reads this address. If you are asking us to delete or send
            you your information, say so in the subject line and we will treat
            it as a formal request.
          </p>
        </section>
      </main>
